00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.903
Oh, the macrophage is here.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.130
So the macrophage, I think macro,

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:34.230
this is like a Greek term.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:38.680
Macro means big, phag or
phago means to eat in Greek,

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.170
so it's literally a big eater

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.950
where it eats up the
virus or infected cells

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.860
by the virus and there's actually
two types of macrophages.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.800
One that causes destruction
and inflammation,

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.370
which is good to fight the virus.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:51.930
Then there's a second type of macrophage

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.725
that actually causes tissue repair.

00:03:53.725 --> 00:03:54.922
(dramatic music)

00:03:54.922 --> 00:03:56.466
