00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:27.693
B cells!

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:42.430
So just so you understand
the whole process of this.

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.830
When pathogens enter the
body, they are labeled

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.560
as antigens and they're
recognized by either

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.300
the T cells or B cells
and then your body creates

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.470
antibodies to fight off these antigens.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:55.410
Now you actually have
memory B cells in your body

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.190
which remember past viruses
that you've been infected with,

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:00.440
and have already an immune
response ready for it.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:02.420
For example, if you get two vaccinations

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.530
for the measles shot,
like you're supposed to,

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:06.970
you have immunity for pretty
much the rest of your life,

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:08.730
like 98% immunity.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:10.490
If you get chicken pox once in your life,

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.900
you have enough antibodies
for the rest of your life.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:16.270
So the way that this works
is your body gets infected,

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:17.930
your immune system recognizes it.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.720
It fights it off, but also
catalogs the infection

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.128
to know what to do if it
returns in the future.

00:08:23.128 --> 00:08:26.461
(upbeat dramatic music)

00:08:27.739 --> 00:08:28.805
(groaning)

00:08:28.805 --> 00:08:30.410
(yelling)
(sizzling)

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.430
So an important part of your immune system

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.960
is actually raising the
core body temperature

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.340
which is called a fever,

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.070
but it's actually important for your body

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:39.850
to be able to fight off infections.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:42.470
Not only does your immune
system in certain cells

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.610
function better when the
temperature's higher,

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.450
but the virus has trouble replicating

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:47.410
when the temperature's higher,

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.710
so it decreases its
effectiveness and spread.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.850
Also B cells release cytokines,

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:54.560
which actually facilitate
the inflammatory process,

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.890
helping your body rid itself of the virus,

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.880
but those cytokines,
those inflammatory cells,

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.870
actually increase your body's temperature.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.154
That's part of their roles.

00:09:03.154 --> 00:09:04.749
(upbeat dramatic music)

00:09:04.749 --> 00:09:08.247
(explosion blasting)
(loud sneezing)

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:09.618
(loud sneezing)

00:09:09.618 --> 00:09:11.286
(coughing)

00:09:11.286 --> 00:09:12.540
(loud sneezing)

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.570
The reason your body has
a sneeze and cough reflex

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.800
is to rid itself of a
lot of these pathogens.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:19.150
The way that actually they enter your body

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:21.180
is usually from respiratory droplets

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.450
being in the air or if you touch some

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.180
of them that have landed
on a solid surface

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.330
and then introduce them

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.600
by rubbing your eyes, nose, or mouth.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.680
That's why we always say
our fingers and the dirtiest

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:33.480
parts of our bodies and
we have to wash our hands.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:35.190
Now you heard me chest compressions,

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:36.920
chest compressions, chest compressions.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.900
But I think nowadays we should be saying,

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:40.460
wash your hands (laughs) was your hands,

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:41.463
wash your hands.

00:09:41.463 --> 00:09:44.295
(yelling)

00:09:44.295 --> 00:09:47.060
(intense music)

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.310
(thudding)

00:09:50.226 --> 00:09:51.600
(yelling)

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.800
This is such a great picture
of the war torn city.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.810
It's something that I
often times try and explain

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.660
to my patients that come in
because they have a lingering

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.370
couch, even once the
infection has cleared.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.450
This happens all the time.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.930
It's called a post-viral cough

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:07.650
or post-viral tussive syndrome.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:11.660
Really what happens is you
have a war between an infection

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.040
and your body's immune system.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:15.210
Now your body's immune
system has won the war.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.640
You're not longer infected,
you're no longer contagious,

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:19.190
but think about the battlefield

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:20.950
and the battlefield is your airway.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:24.660
It's severely inflamed, just
like what was visualized

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:25.620
right there in the city.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.170
It takes time to heal all of that.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:28.570
What happens when your airway's damaged?

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:29.760
You body secretes mucus,

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:30.593
you don't feel good,

00:10:30.593 --> 00:10:32.530
it feels difficult to fall asleep.

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:35.690
You cough, even though you
don't have an active infection.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.360
So it takes time to calm
the body's immune system.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.990
It takes time to heal.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.930
That's why it's no surprise
if you've had a serious

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.360
flu infection, that
one to two weeks later,

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:46.490
you're still feeling run down.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:47.463
You body's healing.

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:53.728
(groans)
(adventurous music)

00:10:53.728 --> 00:10:58.434
(yelling)
(footsteps crunching)

00:10:58.434 --> 00:11:00.738
He's not gonna be able to.

00:11:00.738 --> 00:11:02.186
(silly bouncing)

00:11:02.186 --> 00:11:03.692
(smacking)
(yelling)

00:11:03.692 --> 00:11:05.230
Aha!

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:08.350
Cause he didn't have help
from his naive T cell

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.557
or a macrophage to tell him
how to fight this virus.

00:11:11.557 --> 00:11:13.110
(air whooshing)

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.123
But the B cell.

00:11:14.989 --> 00:11:17.406
(whimpering)

00:11:20.507 --> 00:11:21.550
(electronic echoing)

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:22.673
It's a new virus.

00:11:24.275 --> 00:11:25.108
(gasps)

00:11:25.108 --> 00:11:26.012
Influenza A.

00:11:26.012 --> 00:11:29.429
(intense dramatic music)

00:11:35.457 --> 00:11:37.790
(squishing)

00:11:39.667 --> 00:11:42.080
(yelling)

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:44.460
So this requires the immune system cascade

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:46.210
to start all over again

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.640
with the neutrophils, the macrophage,

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.280
the presenting cells, the memory cells,

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.050
everything has to start from scratch.

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:55.540
You can't just reuse
the same immune reaction

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:57.310
that you had to one
virus for the other one.

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:59.890
Sometimes there's crossover,
but not every single time.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:02.660
This is why we still recommend
that if you have a flu

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.660
during the season but
haven't gotten your flu shot,

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.320
once you get better, you
can still get the flu shot

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:08.320
and get benefit from it.

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.737
(intense dramatic music)

00:12:13.423 --> 00:12:17.006
(high pitched air slicing)

00:12:19.075 --> 00:12:19.908
(yelling)

00:12:19.908 --> 00:12:21.970
The biggest difference we
see with the influenza virus

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.130
and other viruses that
are circulating right now.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.260
I don't wanna say the name

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:28.090
cause I'm gonna get demonetized
just for saying it once,

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:32.330
but for the flu, we have
an influenza vaccine

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.610
that not only prevents it
in a certain percentage

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:37.060
of the time, but also if
you are to get the vaccine

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.460
and still get sick, you'll
have a milder course.

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:42.670
But the biggest thing is we
have an anti-viral medication

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:46.090
that is FDA-approved to
treat and prevent the spread

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:47.370
of the influenza virus.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.180
It's called Oseltamivir

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:51.390
and we use it quite
regularly in my practice.

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:53.530
Actually, if there's a nursing home

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.920
where you have an outbreak of the flu,

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.840
we can proactively, prophylactically treat

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:02.250
the patients who are
healthy to not get sick.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:04.350
Now, if there's another virus,

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:06.810
one that's going around right now,

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:08.220
still don't wanna say it.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.800
We don't have those tools,
it can be quite lethal.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:14.140
So we wanna act smart and
the way we do that is we wash

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.800
our hands to limit the spread,

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.130
we don't touch our face
to limit the spread.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.060
If we're sick, we stay home.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:23.360
If we see someone sick, we try
and stay far away from them.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.850
And most importantly, we
stay alert, not anxious.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:28.760
I put together a playlist for you guys

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:31.200
of some informative
videos about some viruses

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.650
that are circulating right here.

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:35.497
Hope you enjoy them while
staying happy and healthy.

00:13:35.497 --> 00:13:38.497
(upbeat hip music)

